There's an option in the residuals function to save the degrees of freedom for each covariance pair, so if you really want to to a test for significance based on the X^2 distribution that would be how to go about it. The upper diagonal terms or just Cramer's V transformations to remove the effect of the df, and to get a more clear picture of dependence when cut-off values are supplied with suppress = #.

