Date: Tue, 29 Mar 2016 22:57:08 +0000
Subject: six-dimensional multidimensional IRT 2PL model - possible?
Message-ID: <hGhzJt23feE.LUakE7xpAQAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/mirt-package/c/hGhzJt23feE/m/LUakE7xpAQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Greetings,

        New user of mIRT here. From the workshop examples and manual I understand that it is possible to fit a one-factor and two-factor model to the data using

unidim <- mirt(scored.data, 1)
multidim <- mirt(scored.data, 2)

       Is there a limitation to the number of factors I can use? I am interested in trying to get a and b parameters (2PL) according to a six factor model; can the mirt package practically handle this command?
multidim <- mirt(scored.data, 6)

Thanks in advance.

Sincerely,
Colin Wee
Graduate Student
University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign

From u6a75f6f91a59c568 at groups.google.com  Wed Mar 30 07:26:44 2016
From: u6a75f6f91a59c568 at groups.google.com (Seongho Bae)
