Subject: Re: six-dimensional multidimensional IRT 2PL model - possible?
Message-ID: <hGhzJt23feE.6MXUBIuFAQAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <hGhzJt23feE.LUakE7xpAQAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
References: <hGhzJt23feE.LUakE7xpAQAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/mirt-package/c/hGhzJt23feE/m/6MXUBIuFAQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi, Colin.

Why not? If your indicator variables can be explained by 6 latent variables theoretically, you can handle it. but, you have to change estimation method like this

mod1 <- mirt(scored.data, 6, method = 'QMCEM') or
mod2 <- mirt(scored.data, 6, method = 'MHRM')

Seongho

